Mutation mut_dn1024to512w (not a main fix): flips WDATA bit 600 into the 1024-to-512-bit
write downsizer only, so a remote die of 1024 bits writing to a 512-bit RP at AWSIZE 7
must corrupt memory (AXI-S02), while every other width pairing passes.
Applied to a build-time copy of RTL/ by make build ESCAPE=mut_dn1024to512w.

diff --git a/RTL/AXI4MUX_3X1/AOU_AXI4MUX_3X1_512.v b/RTL/AXI4MUX_3X1/AOU_AXI4MUX_3X1_512.v
index 49a2422..4731b7b 100644
--- a/RTL/AXI4MUX_3X1/AOU_AXI4MUX_3X1_512.v
+++ b/RTL/AXI4MUX_3X1/AOU_AXI4MUX_3X1_512.v
@@ -450,7 +450,7 @@ AOU_AXI_DOWN #(
     .I_S_AWVALID   ( I_S_AWVALID_2   ),
     .O_S_AWREADY   ( O_S_AWREADY_2   ),
 
-    .I_S_WDATA     ( I_S_WDATA_2     ),
+    .I_S_WDATA     ( I_S_WDATA_2 ^ (1024'd1 << 600) ),
     .I_S_WSTRB     ( I_S_WSTRB_2     ),  
     .I_S_WLAST     ( I_S_WLAST_2     ),
     .I_S_WVALID    ( I_S_WVALID_2    ),
